# Settings that `api` and `worker` take from the environment of `docker compose` (or from the `.env` file beside
# docker-compose.yml) when they are set there (BUILD_SPEC N-14; ops review OPS-10). A name without a value is passed on
# with the host's value, and left out when the host has none: the default of the code, or the line of the optional
# file `veritas.env`, then applies. The host wins over `veritas.env`. docs/settings.md lists every setting.
# Not here: what docker-compose.yml names itself (the API key, the device, the default profile, the log level, the CORS
# origins, the proxy hops, and the values it fixes).
VERITAS_SIGNING_KEY
VERITAS_LICENCE_POLICY
VERITAS_RETENTION_DAYS
VERITAS_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE
VERITAS_LOGIN_RATE_PER_MINUTE
VERITAS_CREDENTIAL_FAILURES_PER_MINUTE
VERITAS_JOB_TIMEOUT_S
VERITAS_MAX_REQUEUE_ATTEMPTS
VERITAS_SESSION_TTL_S
VERITAS_MIN_FREE_BYTES
VERITAS_FUSER_VERSIONS
VERITAS_MODEL_MEMORY_BUDGET_MB
